From: ghidra_rh850 project
Subject: [PATCH] v850: lower 32-bit byte swaps to BSW on V850E2 and later

GCC's V850 backend lacks bswapsi2, so __builtin_bswap32 can require a
__bswapsi2 libcall even on RH850. Describe the native instruction using
GCC's standard byte-swap operation. BSW changes condition codes, including
a carry result that is not an arithmetic carry; clobber CC rather than
allowing an earlier comparison to survive across it.

Restrict the pattern to V850E2 and later. Original V850 and V850E1 retain
their existing lowering. Keep this local patch until equivalent support
lands upstream.

Pinned base: GCC 78d4ac73dd391005b895a6148cd9831e28e1208b.
---
 gcc/config/v850/v850.md | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/gcc/config/v850/v850.md b/gcc/config/v850/v850.md
--- a/gcc/config/v850/v850.md
+++ b/gcc/config/v850/v850.md
@@ -1043,6 +1043,19 @@
   "not %1,%0"
   [(set_attr "length" "2")])
 
+;; -----------------------------------------------------------------
+;; BYTE SWAP
+;; -----------------------------------------------------------------
+
+(define_insn "bswapsi2"
+  [(set (match_operand:SI 0 "register_operand" "=r")
+	(bswap:SI (match_operand:SI 1 "register_operand" "r")))
+   (clobber (reg:CC CC_REGNUM))]
+  "TARGET_V850E2_UP"
+  "bsw %1,%0"
+  [(set_attr "length" "4")])
+
+
 ;; -----------------------------------------------------------------
 ;; BIT FIELDS
 ;; -----------------------------------------------------------------
